@LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5003
@hubA = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@hubB = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json

### List hubs
GET {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/hubs
Accept: application/json

### Create a hub
POST {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/hubs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Milano",
  "zone": "NORD"
}

### Find a hub by name
GET {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/hubs/by-name/Milano
Accept: application/json

### Search names with the trie
GET {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/hubs/algorithms/trie?prefix=Mi
Accept: application/json

### Create a weighted, bidirectional connection (replace IDs with returned Hub IDs)
POST {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/hubs/connections
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstHubId": "{{hubA}}",
  "secondHubId": "{{hubB}}",
  "distance": 12.5
}

### Find the minimum-distance route
GET {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/hubs/algorithms/shortest-path?originId={{hubA}}&destinationId={{hubB}}
Accept: application/json

### Breadth-first traversal
GET {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/hubs/algorithms/traversal?originId={{hubA}}&traversal=BreadthFirst
Accept: application/json

### Create a shipment
POST {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/shipments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "trackingNumber": "ABCD1234"
}

### List shipments
GET {{LogisticsEngine.Api_HostAddress}}/api/v1/shipments
Accept: application/json
